 :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389982} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd5939b1-d848-5929-803f-0e359be7797a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389986} {:answer/id #uuid "b6b84acd-ef4d-5a5f-981c-075ae5c03184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd5939b1-d848-5929-803f-0e359be7797a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389986} :answer-field/id #uuid "d291aebe-d5b2-53d6-be30-2cb4469d3888" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62b161a5-d7a2-5c40-9b75-1bde2245d5d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-182386" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬(P∨¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, we add a column for $¬Q,$ where the truth values are opposite to the corresponding values in the column for $Q.$ \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $P∨¬Q.$ Remember that $P∨¬Q$ is true if either $P$ is true or $¬Q$ is true. \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,P∨¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nFinally, we add a column for $¬(P∨¬Q),$ where the truth values are opposite to the corresponding values in the column $P∧¬Q.$\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,P∨¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬(P∨¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198260 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c5f2a86-209a-5bb3-a3f2-77d679adb0a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10fd375b-d7d6-5467-8bdb-6f37bc432d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434429} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb4114b-80de-58c7-a9c6-c2e4caceaeef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434433} {:answer/id #uuid "9acebaf5-8307-528a-b69c-75e7d4aa4e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434437} {:answer/id #uuid "9b4b0d88-2d4c-57d0-b244-861d5aa82dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434438} {:answer/id #uuid "c57b9858-4955-5a75-af05-c5a6fbbab5b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b4b0d88-2d4c-57d0-b244-861d5aa82dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434438} :answer-field/id #uuid "74cac60f-4eb1-54cb-950d-4d03ca15d20c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28a2abe2-d607-5ca5-a1d6-25d691cd727c" :question/math-academy-id "q-183378" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n- $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}\\le 9$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $5x-3>7$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have that\n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\le 9 \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is \n${T}_{P}=[-3,3].$ \nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$\n\n- To find the truth set of $Q(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-3 & >7 \\\\ 5x & >10 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $Q(x)$ is\n${T}_{Q}=(2,\\infty ),$\nand its complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}=(-\\infty ,2].$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} & =[-3,3]\\cap (2,\\infty ) \\\\  & =(2,3] \\\\ {\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q} & =((-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ))\\cap (-\\infty ,2] \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-3) \\\\ {T}_{P⇔Q} & =({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}) \\\\  & =(2,3]\\cup (-\\infty ,-3) \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,3].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233616 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57bae420-d529-5b9d-a306-37127c523be6" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Rule of Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f9be4f9-9349-5fa3-b613-a61f24179452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "270" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410223} {:answer/id #uuid "8697752e-5619-5132-bce4-85f1b8da875e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "248" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410285} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1dbebb-e0c2-52a0-8350-bb215802044b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410306} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e38e02-fb12-5161-9fd0-deab260ddeca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "310" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410316} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1bc7e2-fa14-5ac8-9514-f051895c965d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "288" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce1bc7e2-fa14-5ac8-9514-f051895c965d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "288" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410345} :answer-field/id #uuid "46b3319b-2af6-598f-8941-02f6c4fc8ef7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9db0cb85-c477-5f32-9094-207566837840" :question/math-academy-id "q-19821" :question/problem "Peter has $8$ shirts, $6$ pants, and $6$ pairs of shoes. If Peter wears one shirt, one pant, and one pair of shoes, how many different ways can Peter dress?" :question/worked-solution "Using the **rule of product**, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Number of outfits} & =\\text{Number of shirts} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of pants} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of pairs of shoes} \\\\  & =8\\times 6\\times 6 \\\\  & =288.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Peter can dress in $288$ different ways."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233624 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105713 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1671fb4f-937f-5a3c-85b7-7f54f35ea543" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Intervals on Which a Function Is Increasing Using Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef6f08b-f29d-5594-8f2c-27a0f21f015d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288137} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb68af9-b0e1-5c08-a0e2-45ce7c661e5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (1,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288700} {:answer/id #uuid "d9671ad4-96b6-5e07-aaf6-355c5746db9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (1,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289483} {:answer/id #uuid "f26faa92-b721-56e7-a97c-92f2de13d7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289633} {:answer/id #uuid "fe00d6d0-86bb-5bdb-9b05-5f2a986bff92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (1,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe00d6d0-86bb-5bdb-9b05-5f2a986bff92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (1,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289709} :answer-field/id #uuid "65263e38-996b-50ac-b514-9e1f8a99ccf3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "46f89f9b-6749-5057-8b7c-a30df75a08ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-21026" :question/problem "Find the values of $x$ for which the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+8$ is strictly increasing." :question/worked-solution "The function is strictly increasing where ${f}^{′}(x)>0.$ Differentiating $f(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}-3\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}-6x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we need to solve the inequality\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-6x & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above inequality factors as\n\n$$\n6x(x-1)>0.\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=6x(x-1)$ has roots at $x=0$ and $x=1,$ as shown below:\n\n![](images/ec/ec7ea6baa82d60a6cf472c904460190042d889d86cb092b19d9809111bd93b36.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the function is strictly increasing on the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (1,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166738 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e822ac5d-67a0-57b5-b5fe-d3ad03cd91fe" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Containing a \"Greater Than\" Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "145fb916-9aed-5e0c-805d-bdf8e795a910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6672" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410218} {:answer/id #uuid "38ba9fc1-79f2-5b6b-912c-c6c105703d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7798" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410243} {:answer/id #uuid "687283b6-5499-5bd2-b076-a93e5e440109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2202" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410270} {:answer/id #uuid "d9469c50-bd92-5809-9036-77ef3324feb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8699" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410350} {:answer/id #uuid "e40e4629-665c-5952-9423-1e72a8b77087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3328" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9469c50-bd92-5809-9036-77ef3324feb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8699" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410350} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3f83418-67ae-557d-89d1-ea574cfdaef1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e1b12ff8-1521-511b-83f5-03f8cbdd4a50" :question/math-academy-id "q-225084" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(10)$ given below, compute $P(X\\ge 7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0103\\,$ | $\\,0.0293\\,$ | $\\,0.0671\\,$ | $\\,0.1301\\,$ | $\\,0.2202\\,$ | $\\,0.3328\\,$ | $\\,0.4579\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 7)=P(X>6).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 7) & =P(X>6) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =1-F(6) \\\\  & =1-0.1301 \\\\  & =0.8699.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100890 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78dbecb4-68d4-53b0-b47f-f37ce92da896" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Equation of a Curve Defined Parametrically With Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a02222e-7bac-556f-8a59-fb96cc7379fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288430} {:answer/id #uuid "54e72178-1f7b-5214-9ba6-6c902e98a7d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288618} {:answer/id #uuid "86ae557a-8091-5236-b106-cb6c715bfdf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3(1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288940} {:answer/id #uuid "870e697f-06aa-529c-aeec-3d2b85541b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2(1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288942} {:answer/id #uuid "bd1d45d8-de11-5e5a-b944-94183a2a9ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54e72178-1f7b-5214-9ba6-6c902e98a7d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288618} :answer-field/id #uuid "80f53a4c-1f61-543b-a7a8-834f7fc0d410" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "92fe000e-8b10-5f6c-a7a8-e9bb8ce2fa57" :question/math-academy-id "q-24378" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using double angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =(1-{sin}^{2}⁡t)-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{3}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{3} & =1-2{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =1-2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2} \\\\ y & =3(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=3(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "06ab8e3f-2c78-5016-af6c-088a51a16149" :knowledge-point/title "Building Truth Tables for Boolean Functions With Three Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42a353bc-95a0-5521-8bb8-45c847937c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410248} {:answer/id #uuid "fafe84c9-7c27-5298-a0cc-c3cbc0d81e84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fafe84c9-7c27-5298-a0cc-c3cbc0d81e84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410371} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ff6e670-8089-5dfb-895f-29b2e041d357" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/sele